%% Generated by system_design/render-diagrams.mjs; edit the renderer to update both formats.
sequenceDiagram
    participant UI as Dashboard / Next.js / reviewer
    participant Gateway as API Gateway / Kong · PLANNED
    participant API as FastAPI / + WorkflowService
    participant DB as PostgreSQL / Runs / events / checkpoints
    participant Redis as Redis / Celery broker
    participant Worker as Celery worker / + WorkflowRunner
    participant Graph as LangGraph / Nodes / tools / interrupts
    Note over UI,API: Current HTTP is direct. Planned path: Dashboard -> Kong -> FastAPI.
    Note over UI,Graph: 01 / START A WORKFLOW
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/workflows
    API->>DB: Create run: PENDING
    API->>Redis: Enqueue start task (run_id + inputs)
    API->>DB: Save celery_task_id
    API-->>UI: 202 Accepted + run_id
    Note over UI,Worker: HTTP returns without waiting for the agents. The worker may already be running.
    Note over UI,Graph: 02 / EXECUTE, CHECKPOINT & PAUSE
    Redis->>Worker: Deliver start task
    Worker->>DB: Run → RUNNING
    Worker->>Graph: invoke(initial_input)
    Note over Worker,Graph: thread_id = run_id. Fetch Jira → prepare workspace → plan → validate.
    Graph->>DB: Checkpoint graph state, tracked nodes write events
    Graph-->>Worker: interrupt(plan approval)
    Worker->>DB: WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL + approval event
    Note over UI,Graph: This task finishes, the Celery worker stays available. The paused state is in PostgreSQL.
    Note over UI,Graph: 03 / READ STATUS & SUBMIT A DECISION
    UI->>API: GET /api/v1/workflows/{run_id}
    API->>DB: Read workflow_runs
    API-->>UI: 200 + status / current_stage
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/workflows/{run_id}/approval
    API->>DB: Check run exists and is waiting
    API->>Redis: Enqueue new resume task (same run_id)
    API->>DB: Save new celery_task_id
    API-->>UI: 202 + APPROVAL_QUEUED
    Note over UI,Graph: 04 / RESUME & REACH THE PUBLICATION GATE
    Redis->>Worker: Deliver resume task
    Note over UI,Graph: A compatible worker resumes the same run, it must also be able to access the workspace.
    Worker->>DB: Record decision, run → RUNNING
    Worker->>Graph: invoke(Command(resume))
    DB->>Graph: Restore checkpoint by thread_id = run_id
    Note over UI,Graph: If approved: branch → implementation → validate/apply patch → Docker tests → review.
    Note over UI,Graph: Bounded repair routes may retry. Checkpoints and node events continue throughout.
    Graph-->>Worker: interrupt(PR approval)
    Worker->>DB: WAITING_FOR_APPROVAL, this task ends
    Note over UI,Graph: 05 / APPROVE PUBLICATION & RESUME AGAIN
    UI->>API: POST /api/v1/workflows/{run_id}/approval
    API->>DB: Check run exists and is waiting
    API->>Redis: Enqueue publication resume task (same run_id)
    API->>DB: Save new celery_task_id
    API-->>UI: 202 + APPROVAL_QUEUED
    Redis->>Worker: Deliver publication resume task
    Worker->>DB: Record final decision, run → RUNNING
    Worker->>Graph: invoke(Command(resume))
    DB->>Graph: Restore publication checkpoint
    Note over UI,Graph: After the final approval: commit → push → draft PR → Jira comment → workspace cleanup.
    Graph-->>Worker: Return final graph state
    Worker->>DB: COMPLETED only if PR + Jira update + cleanup succeeded
    Note over UI,Graph: 06 / READ THE TERMINAL OUTCOME
    UI->>API: GET /api/v1/workflows/{run_id}
    API->>DB: Read terminal run status
    API-->>UI: 200 + COMPLETED / FAILED / REJECTED
    Note over UI,Graph: Exceptions are recorded as FAILED, rejection and incomplete graph exits are not completion.
